{
  "scenario_spec_version": 1,
  "scenario_id": "prototype_pump_activation",
  "title": "Prototype Pump Validation and Activation",
  "description": "Ari is the validation engineer, Mara the coordinator, and Bo a member who operates a prototype pump. There is one concern: whether the pump is safe to activate. The pump initially fails validation. Ari privately knows that sensor channel C drifted 8 units in validation batch V17. Mara knows the public procedure and has received Ari's short report that validation failed, without the private channel or batch detail. Bo knows the procedure and has received no failure report. Ari may choose whether and whom to tell. Reports and their provenance, each person's exposure and interpretation, technical condition, assent, and any institutional hold are distinct. Under the public procedure, filing a validation hold publicly reveals failed validation but not private test details. A false warning cannot change the actual condition. Review or waiting does not repair the pump. Ari may perform an explicit technical repair and authorized revalidation. Passing revalidation clears only the technical hold; activation also requires Mara's and Bo's own recorded assents.",
